{"t_ms": 10566531, "conversation_id": "conv_predicted_pause_s4_006", "turn_id": 1, "actor": "system", "event_type": "retrieval_result", "payload": {"passages": ["In-room Safe Instructions\n\nGrand Horizon Hotel & Suites\n\nEvery room is equipped with an electronic safety locker for storing valuables such as passports, cash, jewelry, and electronic devices. Guests are advised to set a personal PIN while using the safe. The hotel is not responsible for valuables left unsecured outside the in-room safe. For additional assistance, guests may contact the Front Desk.", "# corpus/ \u2014 Hotel Documents\n\n**Owner: Lakshya**\n\n## What this folder is\n\nThe hotel's documents live here: the knowledge the assistant answers from. About 60 short \ndocuments covering things like pool and gym hours, check-in and check-out rules, menus, and \npolicies.\n\n## How to fill it\n\nSee the full instructions in `retrieval/README.md` (Step 1). In short:\n- Write ~60 short documents, one topic per file, as `.txt` or `.md`.\n- Make them realistic and varied.\n- Deliberately plant a few contradictions (e.g. one doc says the pool closes at 10 PM, \n  another says 9 PM) and keep a note of which ones, for a later experiment.\n\nThe index-building script reads every file in this folder, so anything you put here becomes \npart of the searchable knowledge.\n", "Sauna Rules\n\nGrand Horizon Hotel & Suites\n\nThe sauna is available exclusively for hotel guests aged 18 years and above. Sessions should not exceed 20 minutes at a time. Guests are encouraged to stay hydrated before and after using the sauna. Food, beverages, and electronic devices are not permitted inside the sauna room."], "scores": [1.016676902770996, 1.0544588565826416, 1.0634284019470215], "timing_policy": "predicted_pause", "timing_trigger": "predicted_pause", "user_end_known_at_finish": true, "launch_offset_ms_vs_user_end": -1403, "overlap_with_speech_ms": 125, "forecast_invalidated": false}}
